Dear Hiring Team,

I am excited to apply for the *Software Engineer, Payments* role at *Twitch*. I bring more than three years of professional software engineering experience and an MS in Computer Science from Pace University. Twitch's opportunity to build commerce and payments services at massive scale is compelling to me because dependable backend systems directly enable millions of creators to earn a living from the communities they build.

At Sperse, I architect, build, and operate backend services and APIs for a platform serving more than 10,000 users, using Python, FastAPI, PostgreSQL, and tenant-aware access controls to coordinate over 40 specialized agents. I own customer-focused project deliveries end to end, clarify product requirements with engineering and product stakeholders, and improve engineering processes through design and code reviews, CI/CD, and trace-based release checks. I also designed service contracts and data models for an integration exposing more than 160 validated backend actions, supported by technical documentation and production monitoring. These experiences align closely with Twitch's need for an engineer who can take high ownership of services and deliver reliable solutions across teams.

Previously at Qualitest, I designed and developed a cloud-agnostic Storage Service in *Java* and *Spring Boot*, using PostgreSQL and Redis for data modeling and schema design while supporting AWS S3, Google Cloud Storage, and MinIO. I also built AWS Step Functions and Lambda workflows that improved timeout recovery and reliability across more than 100,000 weekly executions. That combination of Java proficiency, AWS ecosystem experience, and operational ownership would help me contribute to Twitch's commerce and payments platform while learning the domain deeply.

Twitch's mission to empower stronger live communities on the internet resonates with how I approach engineering: put the community first, play co-op, and own the quality of the systems people depend on. I would welcome the opportunity to help creators earn a living by building secure, scalable services with a team that values collaboration, detailed thinking, and continuous learning. I can be reached at #ph or #eml. Thank you for your time and consideration.

